  "2026-10-12T10:53:15.064Z",codex-sol,"Imported only issue 189 with published pm-github using a since filter after a one-issue dry run; atomic privacy-gated import created one item with GitHub provenance. The CLI lacks an issue-number filter. Plan: reproduce the unchanged helper against real pinned CLI receipts, use the public SDK bootstrap contract, and extend source/built HTTP collision acceptance. Publication boundary: affected current source follows the published Web tarball; no hosted or published Web exposure asserted."
  "2026-10-12T10:54:35.323Z",codex-sol,"Exact issue reproduction passed: script-disabled official CLI 2026.10.10 in a scratch tracker with synthetic pm-presets priority 1 and scratch-shadow priority 1000. Unchanged extracted helper SHA-256 ae77965435324d7bf16273f86d580a193c75f3c747927f1bc3dbe19bdeb6668c refused plain list and author equals, but allowed separate-value author and output-format while actual CLI selected scratch-shadow in both cases. Real describe receipt supplied; only process transport replaced. Additional dispatch probe confirms a terminator before list keeps the base owner; list before a terminator selects the nested shadow."
  "2026-10-12T10:56:42.861Z",codex-sol,"HTTP acceptance exposed a further in-scope terminator ambiguity: published Presets interprets operands after -- and can dispatch its nested shadow, unlike the minimal synthetic base handler. Refuse terminators carrying operands when exact secondary resolution is unavailable; empty trailing terminators and ordinary owned local boolean flags remain supported. Unknown local option arity with later operands also fails closed. Tests exercise real npm Presets and both source/built applications."
