  "2026-10-12T12:05:29.141Z",codex-sol,"Reviewer follow-up: local valued options are currently rejected even when no competing command path is possible. Build candidate command prefixes after SDK global normalization, branching on whether the token immediately following a local option is its value or a positional. Prune candidates that cannot prefix an ownership-table command to bound work. Refuse only unsafe owned candidates; preserve terminator refusal and direct collision diagnostics. Extend real source/built catalog HTTP acceptance with harmless values and value/sub-path collisions, then prove the regression by reverting only candidate logic and rebuilding."
  "2026-10-12T12:08:05.618Z",codex-sol,"Real-runtime test adjustment: Presets rejects --since as an undeclared local flag after ownership allows it (HTTP 400 from the pinned CLI), so the same leading valued-option shape uses its declared --display-name flag with --list. Acceptance includes list --limit 5, --display-name 7d --list, values with no owned path, equals-form values, repeated option branches, and list values that can reach the active shadow owner. This uses real installed extension metadata and execution without mocks."
  "2026-10-12T12:12:19.814Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: restore only commandOwnershipError to the PR baseline rule while retaining the new HTTP assertions, rebuild dist with npm run build:server, then run the real catalog harness. Result: 3 tests, 1 pass, 2 failures, 0 skips; source and built both return 409 instead of 200 for list --limit 5. Restored the candidate-path function and rebuilt dist. Initial restored acceptance passed 3/3 with all collision, valued-option and terminator assertions; now running the linked acceptance and both release gates at unchanged thresholds."
